antonio brown managed to take a  situation where he was under contract  for three more years and parlay that  into a new three-year contract that's  going to pay him over 50 million dollars  assuming he's there for all three years  either way he's guaranteed 30 million  plus when he was previously guaranteed  nothing so how did he pull this off well  from the raiders perspective before we  say they paid too much consider how  these deals typically work you take into  account what you're giving up to the  other team to trade for a player and  what you are paying the player and in  this case because the raiders were able  to get antonio brown for only a third  round pick and a fifth-round pick it was  easier to justify paying him more money  now the more they have to give the  steelers to get brown the less they  would be willing to give him under the  terms of a contract so by virtue of the  fact the steelers were so desperate to  move brown that they were willing to  take only a three and a five that  allowed brown to unlock a new contract  that has that guaranteed money that his  previous deal did not have and when you  look at his contract when you compare it  to others like odell beckham jr sami  watkins  antonio brown for now has a better deal  than any of them and he managed to do it  without becoming a free agent without  getting to the open market and despite  having three years left on the contract  that he signed with pittsburgh just two  years ago  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports
 

